libkern arm OSByteOrder defines the plain swap names (aarch64 port, task A15)

The arm OSByteOrder.h gates each OSReadSwapInt/OSWriteSwapInt between an underscore-
prefixed _POSIX_C_SOURCE variant and the plain name. The OSSwapBigToHostInt* macros call
the plain OSReadSwapInt*, but plist.m compiles with _POSIX_C_SOURCE, so only the
underscore variant is defined and every plain name comes out undefined at the libxpc
link. darling PR 1753 drops the POSIX-gated underscore forms and keeps the plain ones
unconditionally; this is the arm header only, so x86 is untouched.

